  "scope": "Repair the two confirmed B14 findings and retain existing authority, storage, IPC, grant and mobile non-execution contracts. No package/Schema/dependency migration, account/transport change, product UI launch, commit or push is part of this repair.",
  "resolvedFindings": [
    {
      "id": "B14-R01",
      "priority": 2,
      "status": "resolved",
      "owner": "crates/am-plugin-runtime/src/authority.rs",
      "change": "Both guards borrow the injected clock before entering Store::transaction and sample it inside the transaction immediately before bound_context. Store waits cannot reuse the pre-admission authorization time.",
      "regression": [
        "context_guard_refreshes_time_after_transaction_admission",
        "capability_guard_refreshes_time_after_transaction_admission"
      ],
      "coverage": "Both guards test grant/session/context expiry independently, including valid-before-wait, valid at deadline-1, and rejection exactly at deadline. Two permanent tests fail before repair and all six expiry cases pass after repair."
    },
    {
      "id": "B14-N01",
      "priority": 2,
      "status": "resolved",
      "owner": "apps/tauri/src-tauri/src/plugins/executor.rs",
      "change": "cancel_install returns Result, reports poisoned-registry or durable session-close errors and still attempts closure for every matching task. The product command returns that result directly. Broker/queued relay reject canceled tasks and state.set rechecks cancellation after acquiring the native authority lock. The closed mobile adapter preserves its no-task behavior with the matching Result signature.",
      "regression": [
        "cancellation_propagates_session_close_failure_and_retry_closes_authority",
        "cancelled_task_cannot_write_after_failed_close_and_storage_recovery",
        "cancellation_failure_does_not_skip_other_matching_sessions",
        "successful_cancellation_preserves_committed_values_and_durable_grants",
        "unknown_install_is_a_noop_and_poisoned_task_registry_is_an_error"
      ],
      "coverage": "Five permanent headless tests use the actual Executors/broker, PluginAuthority, runtime and SQLite adapter. An aborting SQLite trigger injects session-close failure; tests verify error/retry, no late namespace write, continued multi-session cleanup, idempotent success, retained committed values/private provenance/receipts/grants and unknown-ID/poisoned-registry behavior. Four fail before the behavioral repair; all five pass after repair."
    }
  ],
